{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 118, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a missing node2->output edge adds a new path and can reconnect an otherwise disconnected cell, whereas replacing an existing op only swaps capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the direct input->output edge when node2->output is already absent leaves fewer routes to the output and risks disconnecting the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual input->output path where none existed improves gradient flow and can rescue disconnected cells, unlike swapping an existing op for skip."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling a missing node1->node2 edge creates a new path (sometimes the only one), giving large gains as seen when it reconnects the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct input->output edge, removing input->node2 makes the cell depend entirely on node1, raising the chance of severe degradation or disconnection."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node1 receives no input, adding a conv on edge 0 activates every downstream path through node1, a much bigger change than swapping an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With node2->output absent, a new node1->output conv adds a needed output path and depth, whereas with edge 5 present it mostly adds redundant parameters that hurt trainability."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a skip from node2 to output where there was none creates a new information path, whereas replacing an existing conv with skip removes capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Placing a 3x3 conv on a previously empty input->output edge adds both a path and capacity, outperforming replacements of existing ops."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing an identity skip between nodes 1 and 2 with a pool removes a clean residual path and blurs features, so it does worse than replacing none or a weaker op."}], "tok": 18237, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3"